---
// What the author personally owns is the one fact on this page that cannot be checked
// against anything in the repository, and it has not been stated yet. To set it, replace
// the empty string with the true sentence. If it later stops being true, change it in the
// same commit as the trade: a stale disclosure is worse than none.
const AUTHOR_HOLDINGS = "";

/**
 * The conflict-of-interest statement, written as a verifiable negative. Everything
 * claimed here can be checked against the repository or the served HTML. The fund count
 * comes from the shelf so it cannot drift out of date in prose.
 */
import Hero from "~/components/Hero.astro";
import { shelf } from "~/content/shelf";
import Base from "~/layouts/Base.astro";
import { REPO_URL } from "~/lib/site";
---

<Base
  title="Disclosures"
  description="Nobody pays for this site and nobody is paid for it. The interests that do exist, including what the author owns, are stated here."
  asOf={null}
>
  <Hero title="Disclosures" lede="Nobody pays for this site and nobody is paid for it." />

  <div class="prose">
    <p>You can check that claim rather than take it on trust: the site is plain HTML in
    <a href={REPO_URL} rel="noopener noreferrer">a public repository</a>, and an affiliate link is a thing you can
    search for.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="prose mt-14">
    <h2 id="no-money">What does not exist here</h2>

    <ul>
      <li>Advertising, in any form.</li>
      <li>Affiliate links, referral links, broker sign-up bonuses, or tracking codes on an outgoing link. A link
      out of here carries nothing that says where you came from.</li>
      <li>Sponsors, grants, or anyone with a right to see a page before it is published.</li>
      <li>Payment, in cash or in kind, from any fund company, index provider, broker, adviser or data vendor.
      Nothing was placed here for money and nothing as a favour.</li>
      <li>Anything for sale. No subscription, no newsletter, no course, no consulting, no waiting list.</li>
      <li>Analytics. No tracking script, no cookie, no fingerprinting.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>Your light or dark preference is kept in your browser under the name <code>pe-theme</code>. It never
    leaves the browser, and there is nothing on the other end to send it to.</p>

    <p>The site names <a href="/funds/"><span data-numeric>{shelf.length}</span> funds</a> by ticker. Several are
    named unkindly, and none of the companies that run them knows this site exists.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="prose mt-14">
    <h2 id="interests">The interests that do exist</h2>

    <h3 id="holdings">What I own</h3>

    <p>
      {AUTHOR_HOLDINGS ||
        "Not stated yet. I have not published whether I hold any of the funds named here, and nothing on the site should be read as saying that I do or that I do not."}
      When I state it, it will be stated on this page, because a person who owns what he argues for has money
      riding on the argument being right. Amounts stay private.
    </p>

    <h3 id="reputation">I would like the work to be right</h3>

    <p>Months went into it, and nobody who spends months on an argument is neutral about it afterwards. No
    disclosure fixes that. What the site does instead is make disagreement cheap:
    <a href="/corrections/">the corrections page</a> records it working, and an
    <a href={`${REPO_URL}/issues`} rel="noopener noreferrer">issue on the public repository</a> is how you add
    to it.</p>

    <h3 id="tools">Tools and data</h3>

    <p>Every data source is free and public, used under its own published terms: Ken French&rsquo;s data library,
    FRED, SEC filings, AQR&rsquo;s public data sets, Robert Shiller&rsquo;s series, the Jordà-Schularick-Taylor
    macrohistory database, LBMA and the World Bank. Each download is recorded with a fingerprint of the exact
    bytes used, so a provider quietly restating its history shows up as a mismatch. The AI tools used to build
    the site were bought at retail; no vendor has seen a page before publication or has any say in what it
    claims.</p>

    <p>If any of this changes, it changes here first and on the same day, with the old wording left visible in
    the public history.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
